v 3
d driveuse. Use datasets from Google Drive with cross-platform path handling
d
d driveuse finds the Texas 2036 Data and Research Team shared drive (or
d another shared drive by name) on macOS and Windows, sets the globals
d $driveuse and $sf to its path, and loads datasets from it with 'use'.
d driveuse.R is the R version; it follows the same rules and returns paths.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas2036.org
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d New in v2.0.2: driveuse.R searches the same Windows drive letters as the
d Stata command (G: first, then D: through Z:); 2.0.1 changed only Stata.
d The tests cover the letter search and skip the check of this computer,
d with a note, when it has no team drive.
d
d New in v2.0.1: on Windows, driveuse probes every drive letter (G: first)
d instead of assuming Google Drive for desktop is on G:, so a non-default
d mount still works.
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261110
d
f driveuse.ado
f _driveuse_root.ado
f driveuse.sthlp
f driveuse.R
